EXERCISED PATH: model/layers.py:140-149 -> model/frechet_poincare.py:159-211 -> model/model.py:79-80 | Traced the whole chain in the code. The training-only weight table is built once from train.parquet only (train_rqvae.py:256-300: self-transitions dropped at 291-293, ratio (indeg+1)/(n_v+2) at 295, clip [0.25,4] at 296) and bound to every level (train_rqvae.py:329-333). Each training batch carries the global item id (train_rqvae.py:419-423); the level maps the encoder latent into the ball (exp_0, layers.py:145), binds w_i (layers.py:146 -> frechet_poincare.py:131-141), assigns with the curved distance (layers.py:147-148 -> frechet_poincare.py:143-151) and stores (point, index, weights). After the optimiser step the per-slot weighted tangent sums are reduced and applied (train_rqvae.py:441-449 -> model.py:40-80 -> frechet_poincare.py:159-211), i.e. c_k <- exp_{c_k}(eta * sum_i w_i log_{c_k}(z_i) / sum_i w_i). The moved slot then decides the exported SID, because get_indices is called with item_ids=arange(N) (train_rqvae.py:538-541), so the export uses the same curved weighted assignment and not a Euclidean fallback. The same weights also enter the commitment (layers.py:168-170), so both switches are load-bearing: use_behaviour=False returns unit weights (frechet_poincare.py:138-139), use_curvature=False switches cost, commitment and step to Euclidean (145-150, 183, 206-207).
