EXERCISED PATH: model/layers.py:161-175 | Read the curved branch. The weighted curved commitment (layers.py:168-169) is differentiable in point = exp_0(latent) (frechet_poincare.py:56-59, 88-98), so a real gradient reaches the encoder MLP; mse(x, x_q.detach()) (layers.py:170) reaches it through x, and the straight-through at layers.py:174 feeds the decoder the log_0 image with an identity gradient, as specified. The codebook is deliberately not a gradient path (detached at 168/174, sums under no_grad at frechet_poincare.py:168,195; grad dropped at train_rqvae.py:434-437) which matches the "estimator, not gradient path" specification. Every map is clamped: clamp_ball at 1-1e-4, atanh arguments at 1-1e-7, mobius denominator at 1e-12, distance norm in float64, non-finite slots skipped (frechet_poincare.py:21-23, 39, 42-53, 77, 97-98, 199, 208-209); the loss is checked for finiteness each step (train_rqvae.py:426-427). No term is computed and then unused.
FINDING SEVERITY: minor
FINDING LOCATION: model/frechet_poincare.py:56-59
FINDING DETAIL: exp_0 does not clamp its output. In float32 tanh saturates at 1.0 for arguments above about 9, so an encoder latent with ||e|| >= 18 lands exactly on the sphere; poincare_distance then hits the atanh clamp (line 98), whose derivative is zero, silently removing that sample's commitment gradient while the distance stays finite (about 16). At the observed scale (d=32, xavier MLP, ||e|| ~ 3-6, radius ~0.9) it does not fire, hence minor.
FINDING REPRODUCTION: exp_0(torch.tensor([[18., 0., ...]])) has norm 1.0; its poincare_distance to any code returns the saturated 2*atanh(1-1e-7) and carries zero gradient with respect to the point.
FINDING CORRECTION: wrap the return value of exp_0 in clamp_ball(...), as exp_at already does at line 70.

