EXERCISED PATH: train_rqvae.py:340-345 with 428-437 | Read the entry point and the step loop together: model = DDP(model, find_unused_parameters=False, broadcast_buffers=False) at 344-345, loss.backward() at 428, embed.weight.grad cleared at 434-436. Everything else on this check is correct: RESULT_DIR = results/stage2_RQ-VAE/TIGER_poincare-frechet-successor-codebook (line 59) with all writes inside it (63-67, 516, 548), frozen data sources stage1 sentence_t5.npy and stage0 train.parquet (61-62), the export builds raw tokens with the curved item_ids path (538-541), extends collisions and asserts uniqueness (545-547), writes sids_for_hgrec.npy plus the {"item_id": [tokens]} JSON indexed by row (549-551); the launcher hands over to tools.research.stage2.launcher on the frozen port (581-589), and SINGLE_GPU_ENV = "GENREC_SINGLE_GPU" (73) returns early at 564-568 so main() runs one process on cuda:0.
FINDING SEVERITY: blocking
FINDING LOCATION: train_rqvae.py:344-345 (interacts with model/layers.py:161-174 and train_rqvae.py:428-437)
FINDING DETAIL: on the frozen four-card path the codebook parameter receives no gradient at all, while the model is wrapped with find_unused_parameters=False. DDP builds its buckets from every parameter with requires_grad, embed.weight included; no autograd hook for it ever fires, so finalize_backward is never reached in that iteration and the next prepare_for_backward raises "Expected to have finished reduction in the prior iteration before starting a new one. This error indicates that your module has parameters that were not used in producing loss." In the curved branch nothing yields a gradient for layer.embed.weight: the commitment uses .detach() (layers.py:168), the straight-through detaches the decoder input (174), the mse uses x_q.detach() (170), and the assignment is an argmin. The guard at train_rqvae.py:434-436 therefore clears a gradient that never exists, and the candidate cannot complete the Stage 2 protocol it is judged on. The single-card smoke does not catch it, because world_size == 1 skips the DDP wrap (line 340).
FINDING REPRODUCTION: run the four-card launcher (RANK/LOCAL_RANK set): after the first backward, layer.embed.weight.grad is None on all three levels, and iteration 2's forward aborts with the unused-parameter RuntimeError. Minimal equivalent: DDP(nn.Linear(4,4), find_unused_parameters=False) whose forward returns x.detach(), backwards taken twice.
FINDING CORRECTION: make the codebook not gradient-bearing, i.e. self.embed.weight.requires_grad_(False) in VQLayer when frechet is enabled (the Fréchet step owns it and apply_frechet_codebook_step writes through .data.copy_, model.py:80), or pass find_unused_parameters=True at train_rqvae.py:344. The first is preferable and makes the block at 434-436 unnecessary.

FINDING SEVERITY: minor
FINDING LOCATION: train_rqvae.py:398-404
FINDING DETAIL: the codebook is initialised on rank 0 only and the other ranks are merely put behind a barrier; there is no broadcast, although embed is a DDP-wrapped parameter and DDP broadcasts parameters only at construction, which happens before this call. Ranks 1-3 keep their xavier initialisation, so they assign items with a different codebook; the Fréchet step cannot repair it, because each rank computes its step from its own codebook and all_reduce only sums the increments. The exported SID stays consistent (rank 0 exports), but the encoder is trained against four different codebooks. This pattern is inherited from the frozen Stage 2 file, which is why it is not the blocking finding.
FINDING REPRODUCTION: after init_codebook (guarded by if rank == 0), print float(layer.embed.weight.sum()) per rank: rank 0 holds the exp_0 image of the KMeans centres, ranks 1-3 hold unrelated values, and the gap persists across epochs.
FINDING CORRECTION: after init_codebook, dist.broadcast(layer.embed.weight.data, 0) for every level of raw_module.rq.vq_layers before the first epoch.